Note: =====================================================================
Note: from_mml.flow — Phase 39 MML import chapter
Note: =====================================================================
Note:
Note: Composer imports a short PC-98-era MML melody via (mml str). The
Note: returned Sequence can be transformed, layered, or rendered.
Note:
Note: PC-98 common core supported per D-39-18:
Note:   notes a-g (case-insensitive)
Note:   accidentals + or # (sharp), - (flat)
Note:   absolute octave O<n> (0..8), relative > (up), < (down)
Note:   default length L<n>, per-note length override
Note:   tempo T<n>, loops [...]<n>, dotted '.', tie '&'
Note:
Note: Charitable per D-39-19 / D-v1.5-05 — malformed input never throws;
Note: FM operator routing and drum-bank opcodes dropped with [mml] stderr
Note: advisory; loop nesting capped at 16, total notes at 65536 (DoS guard).
Note:
Note: Run:
Note:   dotnet run --project flow-interpreter examples/notation/from_mml.flow

use "@notation-io"
use "@std"

String chiptune = "T120 L8 O4 cdefga>cb<a>c"

Sequence parsed = (mml chiptune)
(print "MML imported: 1 Sequence parsed")
